// minute; ONE BEAT LATER, at beat 15, it reads 66940 with host swap-in rising, which is that
// anonymous memory going to swap. The reading is therefore censored in the same sense as the
// charge ceiling -- the kernel was still holding the workload -- but on the axis reclaim cannot
// answer. Beat 13 is the last unstalled beat: 24736395264 bytes anonymous beside 1895120896 bytes
// of file at zero stall, one minute before the cache squeezed to 13 MiB.
//
// EVERY BEAT HERE IS SeamUnrecorded, AND THAT IS A FACT ABOUT THE RUN RATHER THAN A GAP IN THE
// TRANSCRIPTION. This run predates the seam field on the stat line, so the lines it was read from
// carried no seam at all and there is nothing to transcribe; receipt_peak_seam therefore answers
