// THE DATED SUCCESSOR, AND THE FIRST RECEIPT THAT CAN NAME THE SEAM ITS PEAK WAS ESTABLISHED IN
// (this change's own CI run 35652545009, job 106508550698, srv3-01, 2026-09-21, twenty-three beats
// at sixty seconds, every beat derived from its own `[floor-cgroup] seam= stall_per_min=` line by
// the instrument rather than joined to a neighbouring line by a reader). It supersedes
// gunbc_floor_memory_stat_receipt_2026_09_19 as gunbc_floor_held_set_standing's input; that
// receipt is RETAINED, not deleted, because it is the evidence the 26/25 GiB row was argued from
// and a superseded reading is history rather than a mistake.
//
// WHAT IT SHOWS, AND IT IS NOT WHAT A PEAK SNAPSHOT WOULD HAVE SAID. The peak is beat 18, in
// claim-evaluation-fold, at 26142809464 bytes held. But preparation alone reaches 23.01 GiB by
// beat 14 and NEVER RELEASES IT: anon climbs monotonically from 8.35 GiB with no drop, and the
// fold adds only about 1.3 GiB of working state on top of everything preparation is still
// holding. So the peak SEAM and the demand's CAUSE are different answers -- the maximum occurs in
// the fold, and 95% of it was built before the fold began. A reduction aimed at the peak's seam
// would chase the last 5%; the retained preparation set is the subject.
//
// IT IS NOT A CACHE STORY AND THE BEATS SAY SO DIRECTLY rather than by inference. The file cache
// sits flat at 1.90 GiB through all fourteen preparation beats and is then SQUEEZED to 0.26 GiB
// during the fold -- reclaim giving the cache back to make room for anonymous memory, the
// opposite of cache accumulation.
//
// STILL CENSORED, AND THE POLICY IS WHY. This ran at the live 26 GiB / 25 GiB row with swap
// available, and its own beats record the consequence: the peak beat carries a stall of 11
// faults/min, beat 19 reads 77, and beat 22 reads 3225 while the run's heartbeat shows host
// swap-in rising. So 26142809464 is a LOWER BOUND on what the run wanted to hold, for the same
// reason the 2026-09-19 figure was. A cell whose MemoryHigh sits under the workload cannot
// produce an uncensored demand reading by construction; only a run with no throttle line and no
// swap can, which is the shape gunbc.runner_slot_allocation's shakedown slot declares and which
// nothing can dispatch yet.
